Revision history for File-At

Next
    - Changed openat to return IO::File or IO::Dir objects instead of raw
      file descriptor integers.
    - Updated opendirat, symlinkat, tests, and examples to accept the new
      handle-returning openat behavior.

0.01  2025-11-09
    - Initial release.
    - Thin FFI bindings for the POSIX *at() filesystem syscalls.
    - Helpers open_fd_at/open_fh_at for convenient file opening.
    - Example script eg/at_hardlink.pl demonstrating a quasi-recursive
      tree walker that replaces duplicate files with hard links.
